From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:22:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 107/121] spec: honor min_p in the sampling verify and the RS
 draft proposal

The speculative sampling verify applied only top-k/top-p, so requests
with min_p (LM Studio sends 0.05 by default) were verified against a
wider distribution than the non-speculative sampler uses. Behind
SGLANG_SPEC_MIN_P (default off), drop p < min_p * max(p) in the verify
and apply the same rule to the truncated RS draft proposal.

Also registers SGLANG_RS_DRAFT_TOPK in Envs instead of reading
os.environ directly.

Offline check (N=20000, T=0.8 top_k=40 top_p=0.95 min_p=0.05): output
distribution matches the target (chi2 p=0.28-0.90); min_p on the
proposal raises mean accepted length 1.086 -> 1.174.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
